WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.670
Imagine you fall asleep, and someone
carries you into a room you have never seen.

2
00:00:05.720 --> 00:00:06.840
You wake.

3
00:00:06.890 --> 00:00:10.160
There sits the person you
have longed to talk to.

4
00:00:10.210 --> 00:00:11.790
You happily stay.

5
00:00:11.840 --> 00:00:14.740
But the door is locked from outside.

6
00:00:14.790 --> 00:00:18.720
The philosopher John Locke
told this story in 1690.

7
00:00:18.770 --> 00:00:22.450
So, if that locked door would
have stopped you leaving anyway,

8
00:00:22.500 --> 00:00:24.530
did you stay freely?

9
00:00:24.580 --> 00:00:28.430
In this mission, you'll map
three answers to one question:

10
00:00:28.480 --> 00:00:32.220
if every choice is
caused, can any be free?

11
00:00:32.270 --> 00:00:34.120
Then you'll test Thomas Hobbes and A.

12
00:00:34.170 --> 00:00:34.450
J.

13
00:00:34.500 --> 00:00:38.290
Ayer, who say freedom and
causes can live together.

14
00:00:38.340 --> 00:00:42.680
Your mission: decide whether staying
behind that locked door was free.
